Package: mica-sudo
Version: 1.9.16p2-mica1
Source-Date-Epoch: 1794176058
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: sudo, mica-system
Description: Mica OS privilege for login admins: sudo for mica-admins
 A product's privilege option: Debian's sudo, and /etc/sudoers.d/mica-admins,
 which lets every member of the group mica-admins run anything as root without
 a password. The members are the login accounts mica-accounts makes admins
 (add-login --admin, set-login-admin), the people a provisioning agent such as
 mica-gce-agent lets in with SSH keys; micad's switch turns each off. root and
 mica are no members, and no other account is.
